From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:20:00 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Style: custom properties compared level by level first

ComputedStyleBase::deduplicateCustomProperties compares an element's new
custom properties with its old style's to share them. When the two have
different parents (the parent's style was resolved again too), the
comparison walked every property, looking each up through the other
side's levels and comparing values in depth: 4.5% of GitHub's page-load
CPU time on IRIX, where its stylesheets define hundreds of properties.

A style resolved again builds its levels the same way: compare level by
level, each level's own values, down to a parent both share; equal then
without the walk. Levels that differ decide nothing, and the full
comparison runs as before, so the answer never changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/Source/WebCore/style/computed/data/StyleCustomPropertyData.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/style/computed/data/StyleCustomPropertyData.cpp
@@ -98,6 +98,9 @@
 
 bool CustomPropertyData::operator==(const CustomPropertyData& other) const
 {
+    if (this == &other)
+        return true;
+
     if (m_size != other.m_size)
         return false;
 
@@ -114,6 +117,33 @@
         return true;
     }
 
+    // Level by level: an element's style resolved again builds its custom
+    // properties the same way, from parents that are equal but not shared.
+    // Each level holding the same own values, down to a parent both share
+    // (or none), means every lookup finds the same value: equal, with no
+    // walk over every property and lookups through the levels for each
+    // (several percent of a page's style resolution where pages define
+    // hundreds of properties). Levels that differ say nothing: the full
+    // comparison below decides.
+    for (auto* a = this, * b = &other; a && b; a = a->m_parentValues.get(), b = b->m_parentValues.get()) {
+        if (a == b)
+            return true;
+        if (a->m_size != b->m_size || a->m_ownValues.size() != b->m_ownValues.size())
+            break;
+        bool sameOwnValues = true;
+        for (auto& entry : a->m_ownValues) {
+            auto it = b->m_ownValues.find(entry.key);
+            if (it == b->m_ownValues.end() || (entry.value.ptr() != it->value.ptr() && entry.value.get() != it->value.get())) {
+                sameOwnValues = false;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        if (!sameOwnValues)
+            break;
+        if (!a->m_parentValues && !b->m_parentValues)
+            return true;
+    }
+
     bool isEqual = true;
     forEachInternal([&](auto& entry) {
         auto* otherValue = other.get(entry.key);
